1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This video introduces the AI model posture generator function for everyone.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
In the newly released 2025.0 version, we have launched a powerful new function, the AI model posture generator.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
This new function allows us to manually adjust the joints without any need to input text prompt or upload images.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
AI will be able to simply and quickly generate the model posture you want.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
First, select the virtual model, AI model posture generator in the menu bar.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
If there is a virtual model or costume in the 3D window of the software, a warning window will pop up.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Ask if you want to continue running the AI model posture generator.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
If you choose to run, all virtual models and costumes in the 3D window will be deleted.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Before choosing to run, please save the current work content or open a new project file.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
In the AI model posture generator window, there are two methods to choose from, prompt words and images.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,000
In the AI model posture generator window, there are two methods to choose from, prompt words and images.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
When using prompt words, you can input the necessary description or select a keyword to generate images.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
When using images, you can upload the selected posture image file yourself and directly generate the posture according to the image.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Next, let's take a look at how the AI model posture generator is operated.

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Let's take a look at how to use the prompt words.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The first option is gender. You can choose between women or men according to your needs.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Next is the key word prompt.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
You can enter the description text you want to generate.

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
On the right side of the prompt window, there are three different icons representing different functions.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The first is the key word suggestion.

21
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
After clicking it, it will display the recommended list of key words that we can use.

22
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
When clicking one of the key words, it will automatically be added to the prompt window and the key word will be displayed as a blue font.

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
If you want to delete the key word, you only need to click the X on the right side of the key word under the prompt window.

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Or in the key word suggestion, click the key word again.

25
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
You can cancel the selection of the selected key word.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Even if you use the same prompt, the AI model posture generator will generate different new images every time.

27
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:13,000
But if you activate the second big arrow, which is the key word function to keep the input, it will keep the image generated before as much as possible.

28
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
At the same time, use the new key word prompt to generate updates.

29
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The third type of arrow is random generation.

30
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
When you want to find inspiration or ideas, you can use it.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:31,000
If you want to change the prompt, you can click the icon in the upper right corner of the prompt window, similar to the eraser, and clear the prompt to reset all the content.

32
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Or use the key word function to keep the input.

33
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
For the existing prompt, make detailed adjustments.

34
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
After editing, click Start Generation.

35
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The AI model posture generator will create images based on the prompt.

36
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
If you are satisfied with the generated image, please click Save.

37
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
It can be exported as a posture file for further use.

38
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Now let's follow the example.

39
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Now let's create a new model posture according to the steps we just introduced.

40
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
First, we will set the gender as male.

41
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Then, in the list of keywords recommended by the key word prompt, select the keyword tennis.

42
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
This means that we will eventually show the posture of a tennis player.

43
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Next, we will describe the complete text in detail.

44
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Enter a tennis player's side wave in the prompt box.

45
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Show the tension of speed and the player.

46
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Everything is ready.

47
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Click Start Generation to create the image.

48
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:27,000
If you like the image generated, you can click Start Generation at the bottom.

49
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Apply the posture in the image as a virtual model posture.

50
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
If you want to re-enter the description text in the prompt box, you can click Clear Prompt.

51
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
If you just need to make some adjustments, you can open the key word to keep the input and then update the prompt.

52
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Click Start Generation.

53
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
It will use the current image as the basis for the new image generated again.

54
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,000
For example, we want to raise the arm on the basis of the current image.

55
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
We first click the key word to keep the input.

56
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Then, in the prompt box, add a new short word to modify the posture.

57
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Raise the arm higher.

58
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
For example, raise your arm up.

59
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Once the final image is generated, it reflects the posture you want.

60
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Click Start Generation at the bottom of the window.

61
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Change the image posture to a virtual model posture.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Click History Record on the right side of the window.

63
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
You can check it out.

64
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
You can check all the images generated in it.

65
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:26,000
If there is an image you want to save in the history record, you can select it directly and then click Save in the upper right corner.

66
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Set up the save path.

67
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
After clicking Save, a PNG-shaped image will be saved.

68
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
You can also select all the images and save all the images.

69
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Click Save after there is no problem.

70
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:44,000
The current posture will be translated into a posture file for further use.

71
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Now let's see how to use the existing image file.

72
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Create a virtual model posture.

73
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
We select a woman and then click the upload button.

74
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Select the image to be applied and click open.

75
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
The image will be added.

76
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
After successfully adding the image file, click on the bottom of the window to start generating.

77
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Change the image to a model posture.

78
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:09,000
After confirming that the generated posture is fine, click Save and save it as a posture file.

79
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Next, let's apply the saved posture file to the virtual model.

80
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Close the window of the AI model posture generator.

81
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
You can import any female model from the library.

82
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Or open the project file you want to apply the posture.

83
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Then click on the file to open the posture.

84
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Select the just saved posture file and open it.

85
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
In the open posture window that is displayed,

86
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
you can use the posture file after confirming that the virtual model has been applied.

87
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Use the AI model posture generator.

88
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
All you need is a line of text or a reference image.

89
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
The reference image can be easily created.

90
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:48,000
It is a posture that is natural and expressive when used in fashion, clothing, and exercise.

